      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While vitamin C is a great antioxidant, its effectiveness in preventing kidney stones is limited. There is some evidence that vitamin C may help prevent certain types of kidney stones, particularly those related to excess urine acidity. However, its potential benefits may be offset by oxalate (the primary component of calcium oxalate stones) absorption. Consulting your doctor before taking high doses, a more effective prevention method may involve reducing oxalate intake through diet and staying hydrated.",
