      "content": "I understand your frustration, but relying solely on vitamin C to \"flush out toxins\" may not be the most effective approach, as your body is capable of filtering waste and toxins on its own. Taking high doses of vitamin C without medical guidance can also lead to gastrointestinal side effects, such as diarrhea or stomach cramps. Your doctor's recommendation to drink more water is sound; drinking enough water is essential for flushing out toxins naturally, and excess vitamin C may not be necessary or safe beyond the recommended daily intake.",
